    <figure class="photo-card">
      <img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="SRM University entrance">
      <figcaption><strong>SRM University Entrance</strong><br>A recognizable entrance view of the university campus.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="life">
  <div class="feature">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow">Student Life</div>
      <h2>A campus with its own rhythm</h2>
      <p>With students from different parts of India and abroad, campus life offers opportunities to meet people from different backgrounds, join clubs and societies, take part in cultural events and build professional networks.</p>
      <p class="quote">“Study, explore, connect — and make the campus your own.”</p>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline">
      <div><b>Morning</b><br>Classes, labs and library time.</div>
      <div><b>Afternoon</b><br>Clubs, projects, food spots and campus errands.</div>
      <div><b>Evening</b><br>Sports, events, friends and hostel life.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="guide">
  <div class="eyebrow">Quick Guide</div>
  <h2>Before you visit</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    <article class="card"><h3>📍 Location</h3><p>SRM Nagar, Kattankulathur, Chengalpattu, Tamil Nadu. Potheri suburban railway station is within walking distance of the campus.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><h3>🚆 Connectivity</h3><p>The campus is near the GST/NH45 corridor and is connected to Chennai by road and suburban rail.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><h3>🌐 Official information</h3><p>For current admissions, programmes, fees and campus notices, always verify details through SRMIST's official website.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="section" id="institutions">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <span class="eyebrow">ONE CAMPUS • MANY INSTITUTIONS</span>
    <h2>The Institutions Around SRM Kattankulathur</h2>
    <p>The Kattankulathur area is home to a broad group of institutions from the SRM educational ecosystem, covering engineering, arts and science, medicine, management, hotel management and other disciplines.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="college-grid">
    <article class="college-card featured">
      <span class="college-tag">University Campus</span>
      <h3>SRM Institute of Science and Technology (SRMIST)</h3>
      <p>The flagship Kattankulathur campus, with major academic areas including engineering & technology, medicine & health sciences, science & humanities, management and agricultural sciences.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="college-card">
      <span class="college-tag">Arts & Science</span>
      <h3>SRM Arts & Science College</h3>
      <p>An institution offering undergraduate programmes in areas such as science, computer applications, commerce and business studies.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="college-card">
      <span class="college-tag">Engineering</span>
      <h3>SRM Valliammai Engineering College</h3>
      <p>An engineering institution in the SRM educational group, offering engineering and technology programmes. This is the college represented by the blog author.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="college-card">
      <span class="college-tag">Hotel Management</span>
      <h3>SRM Institute of Hotel Management</h3>
      <p>Part of the wider educational ecosystem around the Kattankulathur campus.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="college-card">
      <span class="college-tag">Medicine & Health</span>
      <h3>SRM Medical College Hospital & Research Centre</h3>
      <p>A major medical and healthcare institution at Kattankulathur, supporting medical education, clinical care and research.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="college-card">
      <span class="college-tag">Other Institutions</span>
      <h3>Polytechnic & Allied Institutions</h3>
      <p>The Kattankulathur campus ecosystem also includes institutions such as Valliammai Polytechnic College and other SRM group institutions.</p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <p class="source-note">Institution details are based on SRM's published 2025–26 handbook and current institutional information.</p>
</section>
